      "problem": "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $\\cos^2\\left( 22.5^\\circ\\right) - \\sin^2\\left( 22.5^\\circ\\right).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x - \\sin^2 x = \\cos 2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={22.5^\\circ}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡({22.5}^{∘})-{sin}^{2}⁡({22.5}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot {22.5}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
